    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0067" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v15/pg45"/>

                <head>15. Telegram From Secretary of State Rusk to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d15-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-03-17T14:00:00+01:00">March 17, 1962, 2
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Secto 53. Eyes only for President and Acting Secretary. Have had brief additional
                        talks<anchor n="1" xml:id="d15-f2"/> with Gromyko alone in connection normal
                    activities conference and will be having bilateral dinner with him on Tuesday.
                    Meanwhile, members of his delegation have shown interest in exploring further
                    with Kohler and Bohlen<anchor n="2" xml:id="d15-f3"/> implications my
                    presentation “modus vivendi” approach last Tuesday. I am not taking initiative
                    for full exploration with Gromyko over this week end in order to give him chance
                    to get Moscow reaction to what has been said already. However, I expect to step
                    up pace of private talks during coming week. Senior member Soviet delegation
                    expressed some concern to Thompson that I might be leaving next week end because
                    he said “Moscow moves very slowly”.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d15-f4"/> I should like
                    to leave open exact date of my return because if we seem to <pb facs="0068"
                        n="46" xml:id="pg46"/> be making any headway on Berlin, that should be
                    overriding claim on my time.</p>
                <p>[Here follow two paragraphs on disarmament.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d15-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d15-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.61/3–1762. Top Secret; Niact.
                    According to another copy, this telegram was drafted by Rusk. (Ibid., Conference
                    Files: Lot 65 D 533, CF 2060)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f2" n="1" xml:id="d15-f2-content">
                <p>The additional talks have not been further identified.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f3" n="2" xml:id="d15-f3-content">
                <p>Regarding Kohler’s conversation with Semenov, see <ref target="#d14">Document
                        14</ref>. A memorandum of Bohlen’s conversation with Semenov on March 16
                    (SecDel MC/29) is in Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 65 D 533, CF
                    2074.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f4" n="3" xml:id="d15-f4-content">
                <p>This conversation has not been further identified.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
